# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# The only secret this project needs. Sessions are opaque tokens stored in the database, so
# there is no signing key to manage.
#
# Neon (https://neon.com): create a project, then Connect → copy the pooled connection string.
# The host has "-pooler" in it — that is the one to use; the direct host runs out of connections.
#
# Local Postgres instead? postgresql://postgres:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/nutriva — TLS is skipped
# automatically for localhost (see lib/db.ts).
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
